+// BM-DOS: set DOS's date and the BIOS clock from the host again, after DOS
+// started.  The board has no clock of its own: when the network's time (NTP)
+// arrives after DOS booted, DOS would otherwise keep 1970.  The frontend calls
+// this between two frames, never inside one.
+void BIOS_SyncHostTime(void) {
+	BIOS_HostTimeSync();
+}
